From 84cdbd260213e2c4b556114e96d67ab375a63ba2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:09:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ga2: code review 55 fixes, round 2

- LoadExecPS2: a program on no registered disc returns an error to the
  guest instead of exec'ing a command line the child rejects; before exec,
  all stdio streams are flushed and every descriptor is marked CLOEXEC.
- Disc changer runs in guest time (30 vsyncs) instead of wall-clock 500 ms,
  and only inserts a disc when the game looks for that disc's program
  (SLPM_xxx.xx), so unrelated misses never swap discs.
- Memory-card entry times use the console clock (JST), like the CDVD RTC.
- GS CSR: bits 0..4 write-one-to-clear, the rest read-only to the guest;
  VSINT latches at vblank start.
- Interrupt causes raised while masked stay pending and are delivered when
  the cause is enabled (INTC_STAT/D_STAT behaviour).
- paraLLEl-GS readback ring consumes finished frames oldest first, so the
  newest finished frame is presented.
- VU1 generator: D/T halt pairs count as MAC readers.

Verified: 561/561 runtime tests, IOP suites, VU1 replay --reference 0
mismatches, Zettai load+save, Mugen 2 Extra Route and Eigou 2 disc checks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
